content.text:
Partly connected. It depends which kind of connection you mean.

**Landing to workspace:** this already works, on FE-B's server. FE-B has merged in FE-A's landing screen and send step. I've opened `http://localhost:3200/` in the sidebar: type a message and press Enter, and you land on the workspace with your message shown. The one gap is the model: the composer's picker starts on its default instead of the model you chose. The fix I decided on is in progress.

The 3300 tab (the `betterlook` branch) still goes to a 404 after sending. That branch gets the workspace screen when I merge both branches at the end of this loop.

**To a real agent or real app:** not connected, by design for Loop 1. Your loop spec said "no auth, no agent calls, no database". So:
- the assistant reply is mock text;
- the preview is a placeholder page, not your running app;
- the model picker uses a mock list and calls no model;
- attach does nothing yet.

Connecting the agent backend (your own keys, real edits to code, real preview) is a later loop. It's also where the eval work starts: tracing every session and checking each edit's build, diff and rendered result.

