- AI-CORE keeps the single list of allowed models, with OpenAI first. The server uses it to reject any model not on the list.
- AI-UI's model picker reads from that same list, so what you can pick and what the server accepts can't drift apart.

AI-UI is now on its next step, upgrading the composer, and will switch over to AI-CORE's list once I merge it.

AI-CORE is still on the agent core (streaming against the mock model). AUTH is building the ChatGPT sign-in flow. The board is updated, and the watcher is running.

